  "about": "Keychron's own raw-HID commands on top of VIA (22 Oct 2026), written only from docs/brands/keychron.md, which cites Keychron's QMK fork (branch 2025q3, keyboards/keychron/common/: keychron_raw_hid.h/.c, debounce/keychron_debounce.c/.h, wireless/wireless.c, wireless_config.h, usb_report_rate.c, nkro.c). Keys, layers, macros and VIA lighting stay with DeviceHub's own VIA keyboard code; this file only adds the A7 'misc' settings (debounce, the wireless backlight-off and sleep timers, the report rate, and since 1 Nov 2026 snap click from snap_click/snap_click.c) and, from rgb/keychron_rgb.c, the lock-key lights (A8 03/04) and the per-key effect (A8 07/08). Each one is offered only when the board's own A7 01 feature bits say it has it (sheet section 2: 'Use these, not the model name, to decide what to show'). Byte offsets count from 0 at the first byte of the 32-byte report, which is the sheet's byte 0 (QMK raw HID has no report id). Simulated only (tests/sim-keychron-via.mjs); never run on a keyboard.",
